    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "If $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}$ and $g(x)=25-x^2$, find $f(g(x))$ and its domain.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$f(g(x))=\\sqrt{25-x^2}$. Domain: $[-5,5]$. Range: $[0,5]$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}f(g(x))&=\\sqrt{25-x^2}\\end{aligned}$$\nThe radicand must be non-negative:\n$$\\begin{aligned}25-x^2&\\ge0\\\\x^2&\\le25\\\\-5&\\le x\\le5\\end{aligned}$$\nThe domain is $[-5,5]$.\nThe source also supplies the range. Since $0\\le25-x^2\\le25$ on this domain, $0\\le\\sqrt{25-x^2}\\le5$, so the range is $[0,5]$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
